    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Omalizumab:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " anti-IgE. Mepolizumab, reslizumab, benralizumab: block IL-5 or its receptor (IL-5 drives eosinophilic airway inflammation). Dupilumab: blocks IL-4Rα (IL-4 and IL-13). Tezepelumab: blocks TSLP."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Asthma:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " severe asthma refractory to step-up therapy (usually high-dose ICS + LABA) with high IgE or eosinophils. Omalizumab: severe allergic asthma with ↑ IgE. Mepolizumab works with eosinophils > 150/µL. Not for acute bronchospasm or status asthmaticus."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Omalizumab 75–375 mg SC every 2 or 4 weeks, by baseline total IgE and weight. Mepolizumab 100 mg SC every 4 weeks (asthma ≥ 12 y; COPD). Reslizumab 3 mg/kg IV every 4 weeks. Benralizumab SC loading then every 8 weeks. Tezepelumab SC every 4 weeks."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Anaphylaxis can follow any dose of dupilumab, benralizumab, omalizumab, tezepelumab or reslizumab, even after earlier doses were tolerated (boxed warning: omalizumab, reslizumab); hypersensitivity with mepolizumab. Mepolizumab: herpes zoster (vaccinate first unless contraindicated). Malignancies seen in trials (omalizumab, reslizumab)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Treat pre-existing helminth infection first; if a new one doesn't respond, hold mepolizumab (Nucala) until it resolves. Don't stop systemic or inhaled steroids abruptly when starting; taper gradually if appropriate."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Start omalizumab in a setting equipped to manage anaphylaxis and observe after each dose. IgE stays elevated on treatment (up to one year after stopping), so re-testing IgE can't guide dosing."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
